# Generated duplicates of the authoritative .ts configs. freesdn/.gitignore
# ignores these, so they never reach the public repo -- but they DO sit in the
# build context, and Vite resolves vite.config.js BEFORE vite.config.ts. A stale
# compiled copy therefore silently overrides the real config in every local and
# Docker build while the published repo, which only has the .ts, builds
# correctly. That is how the image came to be built from a config that does not
# ship: it produced a 35% larger initial bundle (835,723 vs 617,734 gzip bytes)
# and left build.manifest off, so scripts/check-build-budget.mjs died on ENOENT
# before it measured anything.
vite.config.js
vite.config.d.ts
tailwind.config.js
